{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482143-vicissitude-adding-limbs","id":1482143,"title":"Vicissitude Adding Limbs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-28T05:53:46-07:00","id":1482143,"title":"Vicissitude Adding Limbs","content":"Dark Ages Vampire had a specific Vicissitude 6 power to do this but it\u2019s not found anywhere else. As neither V20 or VDA20 repeats this, I\u2019m wondering if it\u2019s an air breathing mermaid, that introduced the idea you CAN\u2019T just use Vicissitude 2 &amp; 3 to do so in order to give you a power to buy. As war ghouls were a thing, adding working pieces of different bodies together is definitely \u201ca thing\u201d that doesn\u2019t seem to require that specific power.<br /> <br /> What I\u2019m leaning toward at the moment is with Vicissitude 3 you can add working pieces of different bodies together with an extended Body Craft roll and a lot of careful work, but Adding Life to Life let\u2019s you rip someone\u2019s arms off and just stick them on your sides and have them work. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T06:21:26-07:00","id":1482146,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure Vicissitude 3 would be enough<br /> Usually I hate dragging &quot;science&quot; in to debates, but in this case adding a limb is a bit more complicated than just rip off an arm and stick it on someone's side; we have a skeletal structure like this for a reason, muscles and nerves and all works for a reason they works like that and while most of the changes could be explained with the Body Craft, Medicine and Science skills as background, a whole new limb for a mortal/ghoul is something I think you need a serious power to modify the brain so it could process the whole thing and actually be able to use it.<br /> <br /> More so &quot;war ghoul&quot; is a bit broad term<br /> A <b>Vozhd</b> is a creation of the Tzimisce, a mishmash of living beings melded together into an elephant-sized, multi-limbed monster. About a dozen lobotomized ghouls are merged through Koldunic sorcery and Vicissitude, resulting in a 15-foot high walking biological weapon.<br /> A <b>Szlachta</b> are a type of ghoul used as soldiers, bodyguards and sentries. As szlachta are considered superior to other ghouls. They are created from either human or animals, and fleshcrafted in order to increase their combat prowess. While this process makes them more powerful, they are also hideously deformed. Each szlachta emerges from its creator\u2019s laboratory unlike any other, since the process requires handwork. Some features are fairly standard despite the variations. A typical szlachta has spikes, armored plates or both. The Tzimisce creating the ghoul removes all unnecessary fat, or transfers it to areas where extra padding might come in handy, such as over vital organs. Most Tzimisce replace the ghoul\u2019s entire skin with something tougher while some add on extra layers to create whole-body calluses or otherwise increase the ghoul\u2019s capacity to resist wounds. Almost all szlachta possess armored sensory organs with increased sensitivity, so as to make better observers - but this frequently results in the szlachta going insane or being permanently crippled<br /> <br /> Contrary to popular belief the &quot;War ghouls&quot; - usually Szlachta - never were famous of their multiple limbs or tentacles, they were strong, monstrous, shocktroops, bone blades, spikes, armours, but multi limbed, tentacled monstrosities were actually rare to see, those were usually the Vhozd-category or belonged to an Elder with Vicissitude 6 at least<br /> In the modern nights living siege engines and Vozhds are rare and the &quot;war ghouls&quot; are usually used in a Siege - and made by veteran Tzimsices of the Sabbat for the occasion, but I doubt they are multy limbed - , aand Pack not really have a few lying around. Szlachta in Tzimsice heavens? Sure.<br /> <br /> In the modern night when the scientific becground is a bit more available than in the dark ages I might allow the creation of a multi limbed creature with vicissitude 3 tho' but it would require months if not years of work (with heavy nerve surgery rolls), not to mention the recovery of the ghoul and the time he actually learn how to use its new limb<br /> Vicissitude 6 power (or coldunic sorcery) bypass this by &quot;magically&quot; rewire the brain and body so to speak<br /> Well in my humble oppinion anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-28-2022, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T06:37:07-07:00","id":1482149,"title":"","content":"Has it ever been clarified what Koldunic Sorcery is employed in making a Vozhd?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T06:48:07-07:00","id":1482150,"title":"","content":"Level 6 ritual called &quot;Create Vozhd&quot; from Players Guide to High Clans is for sure was used <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The vicissitude+animalism combo &quot;<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Birth the Vozhd&quot; </span></span></span>came later to replicate it after the Kolduns a bit went scarce (tho' Beyond the Wall of Death coldunic ritual was designed for a reason - as <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">an attempt to preserve the knowledge possessed by fallen Kolduns, so the ritual in theory could &quot;survived&quot; to the modern nights too)</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-28-2022, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T10:58:19-07:00","id":1482176,"title":"","content":"Levels 1-5 don't let you add to a body, just rearrange what's already there. You could possibly fashion extra arms but that mass is going to come from somewhere. Levels 6+ could potentially do this.<br /> <br /> I heard there is a combo disipline with vissitude/koldonic sorcery but that's the extend of my knowledge on that topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T12:20:00-07:00","id":1482185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482143-vicissitude-adding-limbs?p=1482176#post1482176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Levels 1-5 don't let you add to a body, just rearrange what's already there. You could possibly fashion extra arms but that mass is going to come from somewhere. Levels 6+ could potentially do this.<br /> <br /> I heard there is a combo disipline with vissitude/koldonic sorcery but that's the extend of my knowledge on that topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m aware you can\u2019t add mass out of nothing. The question is whether 1-5 let\u2019s you add mass from another body. PGttHC would imply not, but I question whether that is an Air-Breathing Mermaid, and the absence of the power in VtM in general and either 20th Anniversary line makes me lean in that direction.<br /> <br /> Like I said, what I\u2019m leaning toward is with Vicissitude 3 you could attach other people\u2019s limbs with a difficult extended Body-Craft roll, while the level 6 power just lets you slam arms you just pulled off onto yours or another body and have them work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T12:50:49-07:00","id":1482188,"title":"","content":"I think this is an interesting topic to consider. I've mostly just taken it at face value up to now that adding biomass from other subjects simply required the use of Vicissitude 6+, but that's always been a bit unsatisfying because it restricts so much of the behaviour that is depicted as common among &quot;mad scientist&quot; Vicissitude users to the lower Generations. Which isn't necessarily a bad thing, but it could definitely be inconvenient if that's a character type you want to play without necessarily having to engage in diablerie or get special permission from the Storyteller just to make it feasible. Even with regular Szlachta, you've got to wonder where all that extra bone plating and the sharp bits are coming from unless you imagine every one of those type of Szlachta is being made by someone of Seventh Generation or lower. And it seems like it is more common than it should be unless you imagine nearly every Vicissitude user taking the same 6-dot Vicissitude power.<br /> <br /> I think I have two possible answers to the conundrum:<br /> <br /> 1) This would ironically be a case where I think the regular Medicine skill might be more useful than the Body Crafts employed by the Tzimisce. Without high-level Vicissitude to solve all the problems by &quot;magic&quot; essentially, you have to deal with issues like blood-types being compatible, transplant rejection, etc.; not problems for Cainites, but possibly for Ghouls and definitely for regular mortal subjects/victims. I feel like the Medicine skill might actually be better equipped to deal with those problems than the more anatomy-focused Body Crafts.<br /> <br /> 2) If you can't &quot;magically&quot; solve the problems listed above with lower-level Vicissitude, then combining it with some other kind of &quot;magic&quot; in the form of Blood Sorcery seems like the go-to option. Perhaps have the Storyteller create rituals or Combination Disciplines that allow lower-level Vicissitude to transplant biomass between different subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T18:21:23-07:00","id":1482209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482143-vicissitude-adding-limbs#post1482143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I\u2019m leaning toward at the moment is with Vicissitude 3 you can add working pieces of different bodies together with an extended Body Craft roll and a lot of careful work, but Adding Life to Life let\u2019s you rip someone\u2019s arms off and just stick them on your sides and have them work. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I run it. Vicissitude 3 would let you do something like that, but it's a very long, difficult process. It could months of work. Vicissitude 6 would reduce the time necessary down to a couple of actions. This lets even high generation Tzimisce be mad scientists and body modifiers with their weird szlachta, but this represents a significant investment of time and effort. A lower generation Tzimsce could make in a scene what would take a higher generation tzimsce several weeks to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T12:33:30-07:00","id":1482281,"title":"","content":"Post deleted by author","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-29-2022, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T20:54:16-07:00","id":1482335,"title":"","content":"Grant life to life is a 6th level Discipline and its an extended roll requiring 30 minutes for each roll. So even with that power you can't just rip someone's arms off, attach them and start using them immediately. Using this disipline as a starting point I could see level 7 or 8 would allow you to rip someone's arms off and use them immediately","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}